2026-06-05 15:18:36,674 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Investigation Question Answers
2026-06-05 15:18:36,675 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q1: Was the DC compromised? Evidence of credential theft?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,676 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES — CONFIRMED COMPROMISE.** The spsql service account (with Domain Admin privileges) executed `ntdsutil.exe` via WinRM from BASE-RD-01 (172.16.6.11) at 2018-09-05T12:26:28, attempting to create an IFM dump of the NTDS.dit to `c:\windows\temp\perfmon`. The first attempt failed due to a syntax error, and no output directory was found on disk. However, a second attempt occurred 28 seconds later. Additionally, subject_srv.exe (a malicious service binary) was deployed on the DC at 2018-09-06T22:11:15 with SeDebugPrivilege.
2026-06-05 15:18:36,678 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q2: Suspicious processes in memory?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,679 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES.** subject_srv.exe (PID 5128, PPID 644/services.exe) — a 32-bit service running with 10 threads and SeDebugPrivilege. SHA256: `87c8fa606729ed63cb9d59f6b731338f8b06addbb3ef91e99b773eac2f2c524d`. YARA detected Codoso_CustomTCP_4 signatures (varus_service_x86.dll), DeepPanda htran proxy tool strings, Codoso_Gh0st_1 (UAC bypass), and Tofu_Backdoor in memory. 20+ short-lived cmd.exe processes with chain patterns suggest scripted/remote command execution.
2026-06-05 15:18:36,682 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q3: Lateral movement?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,683 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES.** Three vectors confirmed:
2026-06-05 15:18:36,684 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **RDP (Type 10):** 9,456 events, primary source 172.16.4.6
2026-06-05 15:18:36,685 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **WinRM:** spsql account used wsmprovhost.exe from BASE-RD-01 (172.16.6.11) to execute PowerShell and ntdsutil remotely
2026-06-05 15:18:36,686 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **Network Type 3:** Massive volume (37,330 matches) from multiple internal IPs
2026-06-05 15:18:36,686 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q4: Persistence mechanisms?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,688 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES.** subject_srv.exe installed as a Windows service (PPID services.exe, Session 0). Registry search did not reveal the service registration name, but the process is running as a service with full admin privileges. System event log (Event 7045 service installation) was NOT separately indexed — follow-up recommended.
2026-06-05 15:18:36,689 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q5: AD reconnaissance/enumeration?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,690 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES — CONFIRMED.** PowerView/PowerSploit loaded on base-file.shieldbase.lan at 2018-08-31T22:52:08 by spsql account. Functions include `Add-NetGroupUser`, `Get-NetDomain`, user creation and group manipulation capabilities. Also observed: `tasklist.exe` and `findstr.exe` execution for local reconnaissance.
2026-06-05 15:18:36,692 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q6: Suspicious network connections?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,692 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES.** YARA detected DeepPanda htran proxy tool strings in memory (slave mode syntax for connection bouncing). Codoso backdoor components suggest C2 capability. The htran tool enables network pivoting. Individual Volatility network plugins (netscan) were not indexed, limiting direct connection analysis.
2026-06-05 15:18:36,694 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q7: Security event logs cleared?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,695 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **NO.** No Event ID 1102 (audit log clearing) detected in the Security log (186,972 windows, 311,141 lines). System event log was not separately indexed for Event 104.
2026-06-05 15:18:36,696 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q8: Privilege escalation?**
2026-06-05 15:18:36,697 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **YES.** Kerberoasting activity with RC4-HMAC (0x17) encrypted service tickets targeting:
2026-06-05 15:18:36,698 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - nfury@SHIELDBASE.LAN (SPN: spcontent) from 172.16.7.15
2026-06-05 15:18:36,699 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - spfarm@SHIELDBASE.LAN (SPN: spservices) from 172.16.4.7
2026-06-05 15:18:36,700 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] Additionally, spsql — a SQL service account — possesses Domain Admin-level privileges (SeDebugPrivilege, SeBackupPrivilege, etc.), which is itself a privilege escalation vulnerability that was exploited.
